  "stem": "The function \\(f\\) is defined by \\(f(x) = 2^{x} + 2^{x + 3}\\). For all values of \\(x\\), \\(f(x) = k(2)^{x}\\), where \\(k\\) is a constant. What is the value of \\(k\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "9"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Rewrite \\(2^{x + 3}\\) as \\(2^{3} \\cdot 2^{x} = 8(2)^{x}\\).",
    "Then \\(f(x) = 2^{x} + 8(2)^{x} = 9(2)^{x}\\), so \\(k = 9\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "x = symbols('x')\nk = simplify((2**x + 2**(x + 3))/2**x)\nassert k == 9 == Rational(spr_answers[0])",
